Restore support for Power7 and older (e.g. PPC970/G5, Cell, Power5, Power6)

Revert upstream 5cdeef81ddb4 8331859: [PPC64] Remove support for Power7
and older, and 612f2c0c0b75 8357981: [PPC64] Remove old instructions from
VM_Version::determine_features(), rebased onto jdk-27-ga:

- re-add CPU feature detection and the has_*() feature checks
- re-add pre-Power7 code paths (isel, popcnt, fcfids, ldbrx/stdbrx,
  sub-word lbarx/lharx emulation, non-VSX arraycopy, CRC32 table impl)
- byte cmpxchg via lwarx/stwcx. in shared atomicAccess_ppc.hpp
- gate the GHASH intrinsic on vpmsumb (Power8), not only on VSX
- C1 is_instance_of: linear secondary supers scan without popcntd
- Linux: ignore kernel emulated isel/popcntb, check AT_HWCAP/AT_HWCAP2

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

